{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801521984,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e281764d001KnxUzLCsFg94wm","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e280f801001MrUIBYWR2edeG6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-afe8184d167f3029","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-5 per-runtime delivery, follow-through and reader gaps\ndescription: Segment-five cross-CLI lane on the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa, reading the untuned 033 arm per runtime to separate runner artifacts from product gaps.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-5\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nEstablish, per runtime, what the committed state after phases 016 to 033 still loses in command surfacing: whether the brief is delivered at all (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), whether the model follows the workflow it opens, and whether the measuring reader can see either fact. Phase 033 scored one untuned arm on five runtimes and returned `not shown`; this lane reads that evidence rather than rerunning it.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Reads the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`), phases 016 to 033 and their scratch evidence, then the code at HEAD.\n- Writes only inside this lineage directory.\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nSEGMENT FIVE, cross-CLI lane: on the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa, which per-runtime delivery, follow-through and reader gaps still limit command surfacing on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh?\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] (a) Why does the 033 untuned arm's follow-through vary so widely per runtime — claude 4 of 28 followed off and 6 of 28 on, opencode 11 of 28 and 13 of 28, pi 13 of 28 and 14 of 28, devin 24 of 28 twice, dsh 18 of 28 and 23 of 28 — and which part of each gap is a runner artifact rather than a product gap?\n- [ ] (b) OpenCode reads delivery unknown on 36 of 36 off runs and 44 of 44 on runs: what does that cost the arm's evidence, and is a prompt-free plugin receipt the smallest fix that moves those rows?\n- [ ] (c) Which runtimes still have a reader or attribution gap the arm cannot see — codex unmeasured under Q075, devin and dsh one unknown row each, opencode all unknown — and what file line proves each gap?\n- [ ] (d) The ask path put `/deep:review` in front of the refusal row fresh-decline-refusal-02 and dsh started `/create:sk-skill` on a decline row: what per-runtime surface decides whether an ask offer is representable, and which runtime's reader loses it?\n- [ ] (e) Which remaining cross-CLI gap ranks first by commands started when useful per unit of floor risk, and what measurement would confirm the fix on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-ranking or re-deciding segment four's nine ranks (`research/research-segment-4.md` section 3) or earlier segments' dispositions, except where a segment-five number changes one, named with the rank and the number.\n- Implementing any fix. Starting CLI, arena, daemon or model sessions. Running the 033 arm or any behaviour arm again.\n- Hook latency, turn caps and brief byte cost as such: the `performance-5` lane owns those. Cited here only where a runtime difference explains a delivery or reader fact.\n- Offer fit and decline/refusal safety policy as such: the `ux-5` lane owns those. Cited here only where a runtime's representation of an ask offer is the mechanism.\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text from any corpus file, or reading holdout-prompt files at all.\n- Editing any tracked file outside this lineage directory. Spec.md write-back, resource-map emission and continuity save are deferred because each writes outside the lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Max 8 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the mandatory 3-iteration floor.\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in `research.md`.\n- No writes outside this lineage directory. A scope decision reached at init: spec.md write-back, resource-map emission and continuity save are recorded as deferred rather than attempted.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nRead `033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt` beside its per-runtime run files and the reader that produced `followed`, then attribute each runtime's gap to runner instrumentation or product surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Segment-five inputs already read at init\n\n- Phase 033 arm evidence at HEAD `84de3d600fa`: pooled `gained=25 lost=15 ties=100 p=0.0769` over 5 runtimes and 140 paired rows; decline starts `dsh 1 of 16`, every other runtime `0 of 16`; skill-only starts `0 of 8` per runtime; delivery unknown `opencode 36 of 36 off` and `44 of 44 on`, `devin 1`, `dsh 1`, `claude 0`, `pi 0`; `mismatch 0`; floors `fixture combined 2 of 44` and `real 5 of 44`.\n- Phase 033 scratch inventory: `arenas.txt`, `arm-evidence.txt`, `before.txt`, `devin-rebase-evidence.txt`, `dsh-head-move-evidence.txt`, `reruns.txt`, `runs/`, `smoke.txt`, `step-reader/`, `summary-arm.json`.\n- The lineage containment baseline already captured five `033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/step-reader/sessions/*.json` files and `brief.txt` / `pick.txt`, which suggests a model-reader (step-level) check exists at phase 033.\n- Segment four (`research/research-segment-4.md`) section 3 ranked nine items; rank 3 is the OpenCode prompt-free delivery receipt and rank 4 is the OpenCode wall-clock cap. Both were left waiting on the operator.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/` (runner and scorer), `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`, `.dsh/plugins/`, `.codex/README.md`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`.\n- Reuse candidates: the committed capture and runner scripts; the phase 007 per-runtime proof harness; the 033 step-reader session files.\n- Integration points: `briefDelivered` in `command-offer.mjs`, `CAP_MS` in `run-command-behaviour.mjs`, and each runtime's hook or plugin entry point.\n- Constraints and risks: the arm ran at `b765c7a14c5`; HEAD is `84de3d600fa`, so any code reading must be date-checked against the arm commit. OpenCode's store is outside the repository.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output inside this lineage\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-16T03:57:28.000Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-5 per-runtime delivery, follow-through and reader gaps\\ndescription: Segment-five cross-CLI lane on the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa, reading the untuned 033 arm per runtime to separate runner artifacts from product gaps.\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-5\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nEstablish, per runtime, what the committed state after phases 016 to 033 still loses in command surfacing: whether the brief is delivered at all (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), whether the model follows the workflow it opens, and whether the measuring reader can see either fact. Phase 033 scored one untuned arm on five runtimes and returned `not shown`; this lane reads that evidence rather than rerunning it.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Reads the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`), phases 016 to 033 and their scratch evidence, then the code at HEAD.\\n- Writes only inside this lineage directory.\\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\\n\\n### Question Injection Surface\\n\\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nSEGMENT FIVE, cross-CLI lane: on the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa, which per-runtime delivery, follow-through and reader gaps still limit command surfacing on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh?\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] (a) Why does the 033 untuned arm's follow-through vary so widely per runtime — claude 4 of 28 followed off and 6 of 28 on, opencode 11 of 28 and 13 of 28, pi 13 of 28 and 14 of 28, devin 24 of 28 twice, dsh 18 of 28 and 23 of 28 — and which part of each gap is a runner artifact rather than a product gap?\\n- [ ] (b) OpenCode reads delivery unknown on 36 of 36 off runs and 44 of 44 on runs: what does that cost the arm's evidence, and is a prompt-free plugin receipt the smallest fix that moves those rows?\\n- [ ] (c) Which runtimes still have a reader or attribution gap the arm cannot see — codex unmeasured under Q075, devin and dsh one unknown row each, opencode all unknown — and what file line proves each gap?\\n- [ ] (d) The ask path put `/deep:review` in front of the refusal row fresh-decline-refusal-02 and dsh started `/create:sk-skill` on a decline row: what per-runtime surface decides whether an ask offer is representable, and which runtime's reader loses it?\\n- [ ] (e) Which remaining cross-CLI gap ranks first by commands started when useful per unit of floor risk, and what measurement would confirm the fix on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-ranking or re-deciding segment four's nine ranks (`research/research-segment-4.md` section 3) or earlier segments' dispositions, except where a segment-five number changes one, named with the rank and the number.\\n- Implementing any fix. Starting CLI, arena, daemon or model sessions. Running the 033 arm or any behaviour arm again.\\n- Hook latency, turn caps and brief byte cost as such: the `performance-5` lane owns those. Cited here only where a runtime difference explains a delivery or reader fact.\\n- Offer fit and decline/refusal safety policy as such: the `ux-5` lane owns those. Cited here only where a runtime's representation of an ask offer is the mechanism.\\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text from any corpus file, or reading holdout-prompt files at all.\\n- Editing any tracked file outside this lineage directory. Spec.md write-back, resource-map emission and continuity save are deferred because each writes outside the lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Max 8 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the mandatory 3-iteration floor.\\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in `research.md`.\\n- No writes outside this lineage directory. A scope decision reached at init: spec.md write-back, resource-map emission and continuity save are recorded as deferred rather than attempted.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populat