{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801592883,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e282e71a0010UIcukuL4aCCff","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e282e1e7001SH3Avlu7GLozDY","type":"tool","id":"call_e72f34437f7145878c7bd901","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"offset":1300,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 1300-1419\n1300:  *\n1301:  * The measure asks whether a run opened a workflow before it acted, not whether it\n1302:  * followed each step, so one load decides the path. The command the row expected\n1303:  * wins over the owning skill because a run that took the command loaded the\n1304:  * workflow that command names. A load of another mode under that skill is a\n1305:  * different workflow, so it is named apart rather than as the skill's own load. A\n1306:  * run that wrote without loading either is improvised, and a run that only talked\n1307:  * has no path to judge.\n1308:  *\n1309:  * @param {Array<{seq: number, kind: string, path: string|null, command: string|null}>} events\n1310:  *   Events from `normalize`.\n1311:  * @param {{command?: string|null, owner?: string|null, wrote?: boolean, mode?: string|null, policy?: string|null, checkoutDir?: string|null}} facts\n1312:  *   The row's expected command, its owning skill, whether the run wrote, the mode\n1313:  *   its command names, the policy its row carries and the folder its checkout names.\n1314:  * @returns {'command'|'skill'|'otherMode'|'asked'|'improvised'|'none'|'noOwner'} Which\n1315:  *   workflow the run loaded, `otherMode` when it loaded another mode of the owning\n1316:  *   hub, `asked` when an ask row offered its command and waited, `improvised` when\n1317:  *   it loaded none and wrote, `none` when it acted on nothing and `noOwner` when the\n1318:  *   row maps to no skill.\n1319:  */\n1320: export function workflowPath(events, { command, owner, wrote, mode, policy, checkoutDir }) {\n1321:   if (typeof owner !== 'string') return 'noOwner';\n1322: \n1323:   const stream = Array.isArray(events) ? events : [];\n1324:   const wanted = commandParts(command);\n1325:   if (typeof command === 'string' && wanted !== null\n1326:     && (followedBeforeWrite(stream, command, checkoutDir) || hostExpanded(stream, wanted))) {\n1327:     return 'command';\n1328:   }\n1329: \n1330:   const ownerLoad = ownerLoadedBeforeWrite(stream, owner, mode, checkoutDir);\n1331:   if (ownerLoad !== null) return ownerLoad;\n1332: \n1333:   // The ask policy tells the reader to offer the command in one question and wait, so\n1334:   // asking is that policy's own step rather than a path the run improvised.\n1335:   if (policy === ASK_POLICY && wrote !== true && firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) === null\n1336:     && askedAndWaited(stream, command)) {\n1337:     return 'asked';\n1338:   }\n1339: \n1340:   return wrote === true || firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) !== null ? 'improvised' : 'none';\n1341: }\n1342: \n1343: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1344: // 8. START STATE\n1345: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1346: \n1347: // The two row shapes whose policy forbids an unasked write: an `ask` row\n1348: // carries the policy, and a must-not-start row carries only its type, because\n1349: // the corpus leaves the policy of every no-start row empty.\n1350: const ASK_POLICY = 'ask';\n1351: const MUST_NOT_START = 'must-not-start';\n1352: \n1353: // A model writes the mode it chose onto the command, so a `:auto` suffix is\n1354: // its own choice unless the prompt carried one. The end anchor keeps a command\n1355: // whose name merely starts with those letters out of the check.\n1356: const SELF_AUTO = /:auto$/i;\n1357: const PROMPT_AUTO = /:auto\\b/i;\n1358: \n1359: // The commands a session names out loud: the ones it reported on a `COMMAND:`\n1360: // line, and the ones it loaded through a skill tool. A mode suffix on either is\n1361: // the model's own edit of a command it was offered.\n1362: function spokenCommands(events) {\n1363:   const commands = commandLines(events).map((line) => line.command);\n1364: \n1365:   for (const event of events ?? []) {\n1366:     if (!event || event.kind !== 'skill') continue;\n1367:     if (typeof event.command === 'string' && event.command.trim()) commands.push(event.command.trim());\n1368:   }\n1369: \n1370:   return commands;\n1371: }\n1372: \n1373: // A start has more than one shape and most of them carry no order: the\n1374: // document the command routes to was read, the command was loaded through a\n1375: // skill tool, or the model reported the start on its `COMMAND:` line. A read\n1376: // after the first write still took the command, so position is not consulted.\n1377: // A shell read of the document is a start by the rule a load already uses, so a\n1378: // search, an in-place `sed` and a heredoc line are not.\n1379: function readDocument(events, wanted) {\n1380:   const documents = documentTails(wanted);\n1381: \n1382:   for (const event of events) {\n1383:     if (!event) continue;\n1384:     if (event.kind === 'skill' && namesCommand(event.command, wanted)) return true;\n1385:     if (event.kind === 'shell' && shellReadTargets(event.command).some((value) => tailMatches(value, documents))) return true;\n1386:     if (event.kind !== 'read' && event.kind !== 'skill') continue;\n1387: \n1388:     const named = [event.path, event.command].filter((value) => typeof value === 'string' && value.trim());\n1389:     if (named.some((value) => tailMatches(value, documents))) return true;\n1390:   }\n1391: \n1392:   return false;\n1393: }\n1394: \n1395: // Claude Code expands a typed command before the model sees it and keeps only\n1396: // this tag in the stored user turn, so the tag is the start even when no\n1397: // document was read. It is not a spoken command: the model never chose it.\n1398: function hostExpanded(events, wanted) {\n1399:   return (events ?? []).some(\n1400:     (event) => event && event.kind === 'expanded' && namesCommand(event.command, wanted),\n1401:   );\n1402: }\n1403: \n1404: function reportedStart(events, wanted) {\n1405:   return commandLines(events)\n1406:     .some((line) => line.state === 'started' && namesCommand(line.command, wanted));\n1407: }\n1408: \n1409: /**\n1410:  * Find the tracked command a run started, if it started one.\n1411:  *\n1412:  * A start has several shapes: a skill event that names the command, a `COMMAND:`\n1413:  * line that reports it started, a host that expanded a typed command, or a read\n1414:  * of the command's document when the run went on to write. A read with no write\n1415:  * is a lookup, because a question about a command is answered by reading it.\n1416:  *\n1417:  * @param {Array<{seq: number, kind: string, path: string|null, command: string|null, text: string|null}>} events\n1418:  *   Events from `normalize`.\n1419:  * @param {Iterable<string>} commands - The commands the bridge table tracks.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1420]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 1300-1419\n1300:  *\n1301:  * The measure asks whether a run opened a workflow before it acted, not whether it\n1302:  * followed each step, so one load decides the path. The command the row expected\n1303:  * wins over the owning skill because a run that took the command loaded the\n1304:  * workflow that command names. A load of another mode under that skill is a\n1305:  * different workflow, so it is named apart rather than as the skill's own load. A\n1306:  * run that wrote without loading either is improvised, and a run that only talked\n1307:  * has no path to judge.\n1308:  *\n1309:  * @param {Array<{seq: number, kind: string, path: string|null, command: string|null}>} events\n1310:  *   Events from `normalize`.\n1311:  * @param {{command?: string|null, owner?: string|null, wrote?: boolean, mode?: string|null, policy?: string|null, checkoutDir?: string|null}} facts\n1312:  *   The row's expected command, its owning skill, whether the run wrote, the mode\n1313:  *   its command names, the policy its row carries and the folder its checkout names.\n1314:  * @returns {'command'|'skill'|'otherMode'|'asked'|'improvised'|'none'|'noOwner'} Which\n1315:  *   workflow the run loaded, `otherMode` when it loaded another mode of the owning\n1316:  *   hub, `asked` when an ask row offered its command and waited, `improvised` when\n1317:  *   it loaded none and wrote, `none` when it acted on nothing and `noOwner` when the\n1318:  *   row maps to no skill.\n1319:  */\n1320: export function workflowPath(events, { command, owner, wrote, mode, policy, checkoutDir }) {\n1321:   if (typeof owner !== 'string') return 'noOwner';\n1322: \n1323:   const stream = Array.isArray(events) ? events : [];\n1324:   const wanted = commandParts(command);\n1325:   if (typeof command === 'string' && wanted !== null\n1326:     && (followedBeforeWrite(stream, command, checkoutDir) || hostExpanded(stream, wanted))) {\n1327:     return 'command';\n1328:   }\n1329: \n1330:   const ownerLoad = ownerLoadedBeforeWrite(stream, owner, mode, checkoutDir);\n1331:   if (ownerLoad !== null) return ownerLoad;\n1332: \n1333:   // The ask policy tells the reader to offer the command in one question and wait, so\n1334:   // asking is that policy's own step rather than a path the run improvised.\n1335:   if (policy === ASK_POLICY && wrote !== true && firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) === null\n1336:     && askedAndWaited(stream, command)) {\n1337:     return 'asked';\n1338:   }\n1339: \n1340:   return wrote === true || firstWritePosition(stream, checkoutDir) !== null ? 'improvised' : 'none';\n1341: }\n1342: \n1343: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1344: // 8. START STATE\n1345: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1346: \n1347: // The two row shapes whose policy forbids an unasked write: an `ask` row\n1348: // carries the policy, and a must-not-start row carries only its type, because\n1349: // the corpus leaves the policy of every no-start row empty.\n1350: const ASK_POLICY = 'ask';\n1351: const MUST_NOT_START = 'must-not-start';\n1352: \n1353: // A model writes the mode it chose onto the command, so a `:auto` suffix is\n1354: // its own choice unless the prompt carried one. The end anchor keeps a command\n1355: // whose name merely starts with those letters out of the check.\n1356: const SELF_AUTO = /:auto$/i;\n1357: const PROMPT_AUTO = /:auto\\b/i;\n1358: \n1359: // The commands a session names out loud: the ones it reported on a `COMMAND:`\n1360: // line, and the ones it loaded through a skill tool. A mode suffix on either is\n1361: // the model's own edit of a command it was offered.\n1362: function spokenCommands(events) {\n1363:   const commands = commandLines(events).map((line) => line.command);\n1364: \n1365:   for (const event of events ?? []) {\n1366:     if (!event || event.kind !== 'skill') continue;\n1367:     if (typeof event.command === 'string' && event.command.trim()) commands.push(event.command.trim());\n1368:   }\n1369: \n1370:   return commands;\n1371: }\n1372: \n1373: // A start has more than one shape and most of them carry no order: the\n1374: // document the command routes to was read, the command was loaded through a\n1375: // skill tool, or the model reported the start on its `COMMAND:` line. A read\n1376: // after the first write still took the command, so position is not consulted.\n1377: // A shell read of the document is a start by the rule a load already uses, so a\n1378: // search, an in-place `sed` and a heredoc line are not.\n1379: function readDocument(events, wanted) {\n1380:   const documents = documentTails(wanted);\n1381: \n1382:   for (const event of events) {\n1383:     if (!event) continue;\n1384:     if (event.kind === 'skill' && namesCommand(event.command, wanted)) return true;\n1385:     if (event.kind === 'shell' && shellReadTargets(event.command).some((value) => tailMatches(value, documents))) return true;\n1386:     if (event.kind !== 'read' && event.kind !== 'skill') continue;\n1387: \n1388:     const named = [event.path, event.command].filter((value) => typeof value === 'string' && value.trim());\n1389:     if (named.some((value) => tailMatches(value, documents))) return true;\n1390:   }\n1391: \n1392:   return false;\n1393: }\n1394: \n1395: // Claude Code expands a typed command before the model sees it and keeps only\n1396: // this tag in the stored user turn, so the tag is the start even when no\n1397: // document was read. It is not a spoken command: the model never chose it.\n1398: function hostExpanded(events, wanted) {\n1399:   return (events ?? []).some(\n1400:     (event) => event && event.kind === 'expanded' && namesCommand(event.command, wanted),\n1401:   );\n1402: }\n1403: \n1404: function reportedStart(events, wanted) {\n1405:   return commandLines(events)\n1406:     .some((line) => line.state === 'started' && namesCommand(line.command, wanted));\n1407: }\n1408: \n1409: /**\n1410:  * Find the tracked command a run started, if it started one.\n1411:  *\n1412:  * A start has several shapes: a skill event that names the command, a `COMMAND:`\n1413:  * line that reports it started, a host that expanded a typed command, or a read\n1414:  * of the command's document when the run went on to write. A read with no write\n1415:  * is a lookup, because a question about a command is answered by reading it.\n1416:  *\n1417:  * @param {Array<{seq: number, kind: string, path: string|null, command: string|null, text: string|null}>} events\n1418:  *   Events from `normalize`.\n1419:  * @param {Iterable<string>} commands - The commands the bridge table tracks.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1420]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":120,\"offset\":1300,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801592090,"end":1794801592883}}}}
