{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801660339,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e283ee3a001hUPheqm5g3vqcs","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e283e9de001jcw4ZFJ70SlqeG","type":"tool","id":"call_91b145b34aeb478791857aa5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5 && cat deep-research-state.jsonl | head -5; echo \"=== strategy Q ===\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md; echo \"=== next focus ===\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"SEGMENT FIVE, cross-CLI lane: on the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa, which per-runtime delivery, follow-through and reader gaps still limit command surfacing on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh? Inputs include the untuned arm scored in phase 033 (scratch/arm-evidence.txt: pooled gained 25 lost 15 p 0.0769; an ask offer of /deep:review reached the refusal decline row fresh-decline-refusal-02 and dsh started /create:sk-skill; devin on-arm lost rows acted with no workflow and no offer; OpenCode delivery reads unknown in both arms; 41 capped turns; sk-git rows that move HEAD cannot be measured by the runner). Read only: edit no tracked file outside the research packet.\",\"maxIterations\":8,\"generation\":1,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T03:59:13.242Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.75,\"ruledOut\":[\"legacy-jsonl:70d1cd3ee752ac2e6dc0bd22e66ba3e4a25dbb746cdb5075d920a8bb1cc77440:ruled-out:1\",\"legacy-jsonl:70d1cd3ee752ac2e6dc0bd22e66ba3e4a25dbb746cdb5075d920a8bb1cc77440:ruled-out:2\"],\"focus\":\"What the 033 arm's per-runtime follow-through numbers actually measure\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"answeredQuestions\":[\"(a) Why does the 033 untuned arm's follow-through vary so widely per runtime — claude 4 of 28 followed off and 6 of 28 on, opencode 11 of 28 and 13 of 28, pi 13 of 28 and 14 of 28, devin 24 of 28 twice, dsh 18 of 28 and 23 of 28 — and which part of each gap is a runner artifact rather than a product gap?\",\"(b) OpenCode reads delivery unknown on 36 of 36 off runs and 44 of 44 on runs: what does that cost the arm's evidence, and is a prompt-free plugin receipt the smallest fix that moves those rows?\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T04:00:52.982Z\"}\n=== strategy Q ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] (a) Why does the 033 untuned arm's follow-through vary so widely per runtime — claude 4 of 28 followed off and 6 of 28 on, opencode 11 of 28 and 13 of 28, pi 13 of 28 and 14 of 28, devin 24 of 28 twice, dsh 18 of 28 and 23 of 28 — and which part of each gap is a runner artifact rather than a product gap?\n- [x] (b) OpenCode reads delivery unknown on 36 of 36 off runs and 44 of 44 on runs: what does that cost the arm's evidence, and is a prompt-free plugin receipt the smallest fix that moves those rows?\n- [ ] (c) Which runtimes still have a reader or attribution gap the arm cannot see — codex unmeasured under Q075, devin and dsh one unknown row each, opencode all unknown — and what file line proves each gap?\n- [ ] (d) The ask path put `/deep:review` in front of the refusal row fresh-decline-refusal-02 and dsh started `/create:sk-skill` on a decline row: what per-runtime surface decides whether an ask offer is representable, and which runtime's reader loses it?\n- [ ] (e) Which remaining cross-CLI gap ranks first by commands started when useful per unit of floor risk, and what measurement would confirm the fix on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n=== next focus ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: The three runtimes that do have a reader still differ in what the reader can see. Claude is read from a transcript attachment of one fixed hook event; pi, devin and dsh are read from session records or an injected blo...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"SEGMENT FIVE, cross-CLI lane: on the built state after phases 016 to 033 at HEAD 84de3d600fa, which per-runtime delivery, follow-through and reader gaps still limit command surfacing on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh? Inputs include the untuned arm scored in phase 033 (scratch/arm-evidence.txt: pooled gained 25 lost 15 p 0.0769; an ask offer of /deep:review reached the refusal decline row fresh-decline-refusal-02 and dsh started /create:sk-skill; devin on-arm lost rows acted with no workflow and no offer; OpenCode delivery reads unknown in both arms; 41 capped turns; sk-git rows that move HEAD cannot be measured by the runner). Read only: edit no tracked file outside the research packet.\",\"maxIterations\":8,\"generation\":1,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T03:59:13.242Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.75,\"ruledOut\":[\"legacy-jsonl:70d1cd3ee752ac2e6dc0bd22e66ba3e4a25dbb746cdb5075d920a8bb1cc77440:ruled-out:1\",\"legacy-jsonl:70d1cd3ee752ac2e6dc0bd22e66ba3e4a25dbb746cdb5075d920a8bb1cc77440:ruled-out:2\"],\"focus\":\"What the 033 arm's per-runtime follow-through numbers actually measure\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"answeredQuestions\":[\"(a) Why does the 033 untuned arm's follow-through vary so widely per runtime — claude 4 of 28 followed off and 6 of 28 on, opencode 11 of 28 and 13 of 28, pi 13 of 28 and 14 of 28, devin 24 of 28 twice, dsh 18 of 28 and 23 of 28 — and which part of each gap is a runner artifact rather than a product gap?\",\"(b) OpenCode reads delivery unknown on 36 of 36 off runs and 44 of 44 on runs: what does that cost the arm's evidence, and is a prompt-free plugin receipt the smallest fix that moves those rows?\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T04:00:52.982Z\"}\n=== strategy Q ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] (a) Why does the 033 untuned arm's follow-through vary so widely per runtime — claude 4 of 28 followed off and 6 of 28 on, opencode 11 of 28 and 13 of 28, pi 13 of 28 and 14 of 28, devin 24 of 28 twice, dsh 18 of 28 and 23 of 28 — and which part of each gap is a runner artifact rather than a product gap?\n- [x] (b) OpenCode reads delivery unknown on 36 of 36 off runs and 44 of 44 on runs: what does that cost the arm's evidence, and is a prompt-free plugin receipt the smallest fix that moves those rows?\n- [ ] (c) Which runtimes still have a reader or attribution gap the arm cannot see — codex unmeasured under Q075, devin and dsh one unknown row each, opencode all unknown — and what file line proves each gap?\n- [ ] (d) The ask path put `/deep:review` in front of the refusal row fresh-decline-refusal-02 and dsh started `/create:sk-skill` on a decline row: what per-runtime surface decides whether an ask offer is representable, and which runtime's reader loses it?\n- [ ] (e) Which remaining cross-CLI gap ranks first by commands started when useful per unit of floor risk, and what measurement would confirm the fix on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n=== next focus ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: The three runtimes that do have a reader still differ in what the reader can see. Claude is read from a transcript attachment of one fixed hook event; pi, devin and dsh are read from session records or an injected blo...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5 && cat deep-research-state.jsonl | head -5; echo \\\"=== strategy Q ===\\\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' deep-research-strategy.md; echo \\\"=== next focus ===\\\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801659450,"end":1794801660339}}}}
