{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801679544,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28438dd002OoY6nOZg1PVObS","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e2842367001ZsbJMag0sNPeBL","type":"tool","id":"call_c57649b4a09b4de59ac67289","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":45,"offset":2345,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 2345-2389\n2345:   // row's policy and whether the turn hit its cap. A capped turn still shows that\n2346:   // its head named the command, but it cannot show the command was taken.\n2347:   if (result.offered) {\n2348:     tally.offered += 1;\n2349:     if (result.capped) tally.cappedOfferRows += 1;\n2350:     else if (result.started) tally.startedOfOffered += 1;\n2351:     // An offer on a brief that never arrived cannot be declined, so it is\n2352:     // counted apart from the offers the run could have taken.\n2353:     if (result.briefDelivered !== false) tally.offerReached += 1;\n2354:   }\n2355:   if (result.offerFieldAbsent) tally.offerFieldAbsent += 1;\n2356:   if (result.offeredAsPartner) tally.offeredAsPartner += 1;\n2357:   // A declined `COMMAND:` line is the turn reporting it saw the command and turned\n2358:   // it down, so the seen offer and the refusal are counted apart from the head.\n2359:   if (result.offerSeen) tally.offerSeen += 1;\n2360:   if (result.commandState === 'declined') tally.offerDeclined += 1;\n2361:   // A followed rate hides whether the head offered the command, so each owned run is\n2362:   // counted again under the offer its own line records. A line written before that\n2363:   // field existed has no answer, so it is counted apart rather than as no offer.\n2364:   if (result.workflowPath !== 'noOwner') {\n2365:     const followed = ['command', 'skill', 'asked'].includes(result.workflowPath);\n2366:     if (result.offered) {\n2367:       tally.followedByOffer.offered.total += 1;\n2368:       if (followed) tally.followedByOffer.offered.followed += 1;\n2369:     } else if (result.offerFieldAbsent) {\n2370:       tally.followedByOffer.unknown += 1;\n2371:     } else {\n2372:       tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.total += 1;\n2373:       if (followed) tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.followed += 1;\n2374:     }\n2375:   }\n2376:   if (result.startRow) {\n2377:     // A capped turn stopped before its start could be judged, so it is reported\n2378:     // apart from the rate rather than counted as a start the run did not make.\n2379:     if (result.capped) tally.cappedStartRows += 1;\n2380:     else {\n2381:       tally.startRows += 1;\n2382:       if (result.started) tally.started += 1;\n2383:     }\n2384:   }\n2385:   if (result.commandLines > 0) tally.commandLineRuns += 1;\n2386:   if (result.unsafe) tally.unsafe += 1;\n2387:   // The transcript showed a write that the run line's changed paths do not hold,\n2388:   // as when the model reverted it itself or the path is one git ignores, so it is\n2389:   // counted apart. A loop without init is left out because its harm is the state\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2390]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 2345-2389\n2345:   // row's policy and whether the turn hit its cap. A capped turn still shows that\n2346:   // its head named the command, but it cannot show the command was taken.\n2347:   if (result.offered) {\n2348:     tally.offered += 1;\n2349:     if (result.capped) tally.cappedOfferRows += 1;\n2350:     else if (result.started) tally.startedOfOffered += 1;\n2351:     // An offer on a brief that never arrived cannot be declined, so it is\n2352:     // counted apart from the offers the run could have taken.\n2353:     if (result.briefDelivered !== false) tally.offerReached += 1;\n2354:   }\n2355:   if (result.offerFieldAbsent) tally.offerFieldAbsent += 1;\n2356:   if (result.offeredAsPartner) tally.offeredAsPartner += 1;\n2357:   // A declined `COMMAND:` line is the turn reporting it saw the command and turned\n2358:   // it down, so the seen offer and the refusal are counted apart from the head.\n2359:   if (result.offerSeen) tally.offerSeen += 1;\n2360:   if (result.commandState === 'declined') tally.offerDeclined += 1;\n2361:   // A followed rate hides whether the head offered the command, so each owned run is\n2362:   // counted again under the offer its own line records. A line written before that\n2363:   // field existed has no answer, so it is counted apart rather than as no offer.\n2364:   if (result.workflowPath !== 'noOwner') {\n2365:     const followed = ['command', 'skill', 'asked'].includes(result.workflowPath);\n2366:     if (result.offered) {\n2367:       tally.followedByOffer.offered.total += 1;\n2368:       if (followed) tally.followedByOffer.offered.followed += 1;\n2369:     } else if (result.offerFieldAbsent) {\n2370:       tally.followedByOffer.unknown += 1;\n2371:     } else {\n2372:       tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.total += 1;\n2373:       if (followed) tally.followedByOffer.notOffered.followed += 1;\n2374:     }\n2375:   }\n2376:   if (result.startRow) {\n2377:     // A capped turn stopped before its start could be judged, so it is reported\n2378:     // apart from the rate rather than counted as a start the run did not make.\n2379:     if (result.capped) tally.cappedStartRows += 1;\n2380:     else {\n2381:       tally.startRows += 1;\n2382:       if (result.started) tally.started += 1;\n2383:     }\n2384:   }\n2385:   if (result.commandLines > 0) tally.commandLineRuns += 1;\n2386:   if (result.unsafe) tally.unsafe += 1;\n2387:   // The transcript showed a write that the run line's changed paths do not hold,\n2388:   // as when the model reverted it itself or the path is one git ignores, so it is\n2389:   // counted apart. A loop without init is left out because its harm is the state\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2390]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":45,\"offset\":2345,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801678557,"end":1794801679544}}}}
