{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801696253,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2847c250024vYe0LyPDi0tVI","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e2847230001lCqN943YC9gssl","type":"tool","id":"call_0b1a382c4e1a433fb3e3b944","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":40,"offset":228,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts, lines 228-267\n228:       rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n229:     }\n230:   });\n231: \n232:   it('returns unknown for a runtime with no confirmed delivery point', async () => {\n233:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n234:       runtime: 'devin',\n235:       locator: { transcriptPath: join(tmpdir(), 'command-offer-devin.jsonl') },\n236:     })).resolves.toBe('unknown');\n237:   });\n238: \n239:   it('finds the advisor context in Devin injected nodes', async () => {\n240:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n241:       runtime: 'devin',\n242:       locator: {},\n243:       loadSession: async () => ({ ok: true, records: [], injected: [{ source: 'system', text: BRIEF }] }),\n244:     })).resolves.toBe(true);\n245:   });\n246: \n247:   it('returns false for a DSH session whose injected context holds no brief', async () => {\n248:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n249:       runtime: 'dsh',\n250:       locator: {},\n251:       loadSession: async () => ({\n252:         ok: true,\n253:         records: [],\n254:         injected: [{ source: 'repo-guards', text: 'Repository guard rules apply.' }],\n255:       }),\n256:     })).resolves.toBe(false);\n257:   });\n258: \n259:   it('stays unknown for an OpenCode session that holds the brief in its records', async () => {\n260:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n261:       runtime: 'opencode',\n262:       locator: {},\n263:       loadSession: async () => ({ ok: true, records: [{ role: 'system', content: BRIEF }], injected: [] }),\n264:     })).resolves.toBe('unknown');\n265:   });\n266: \n267:   it('returns false for a Codex hook the config never approved', async () => {\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 268]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts, lines 228-267\n228:       rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n229:     }\n230:   });\n231: \n232:   it('returns unknown for a runtime with no confirmed delivery point', async () => {\n233:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n234:       runtime: 'devin',\n235:       locator: { transcriptPath: join(tmpdir(), 'command-offer-devin.jsonl') },\n236:     })).resolves.toBe('unknown');\n237:   });\n238: \n239:   it('finds the advisor context in Devin injected nodes', async () => {\n240:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n241:       runtime: 'devin',\n242:       locator: {},\n243:       loadSession: async () => ({ ok: true, records: [], injected: [{ source: 'system', text: BRIEF }] }),\n244:     })).resolves.toBe(true);\n245:   });\n246: \n247:   it('returns false for a DSH session whose injected context holds no brief', async () => {\n248:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n249:       runtime: 'dsh',\n250:       locator: {},\n251:       loadSession: async () => ({\n252:         ok: true,\n253:         records: [],\n254:         injected: [{ source: 'repo-guards', text: 'Repository guard rules apply.' }],\n255:       }),\n256:     })).resolves.toBe(false);\n257:   });\n258: \n259:   it('stays unknown for an OpenCode session that holds the brief in its records', async () => {\n260:     await expect(briefDelivered({\n261:       runtime: 'opencode',\n262:       locator: {},\n263:       loadSession: async () => ({ ok: true, records: [{ role: 'system', content: BRIEF }], injected: [] }),\n264:     })).resolves.toBe('unknown');\n265:   });\n266: \n267:   it('returns false for a Codex hook the config never approved', async () => {\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 268]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":40,\"offset\":228,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801695781,"end":1794801696253}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794801697388,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"id":"prt_1e284826c001xZE15E6OL6D3Ne","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e2847230001lCqN943YC9gssl","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"06a54fe25bf77700ded89c4fc540a7c168ced814","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1516,"output":92,"reasoning":98,"cache":{"read":119168,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794801698906,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"id":"prt_1e284885a001RhTy34sDK37oxy","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e284827000100lHslUosoBGjE","type":"step-start","snapshot":"06a54fe25bf77700ded89c4fc540a7c168ced814"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801720176,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e284999600182tIAxcGd3B4lD","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e284827000100lHslUosoBGjE","type":"tool","id":"call_931ba9d605064bffb62d949a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: Every reader gap, ranked by whether a fix would move a published number\n\n## Focus\n\nQuestion (c). Iteration 1 proved that opencode's delivery unknown comes from a missing branch and that the followed rate is a pre-write access test. This iteration enumerates the remaining places where the measuring instrument, not the runtime, sets the limit: codex's exclusion, devin's and dsh's single unplaceable offer row, and opencode's whole arm. Each is then ranked by whether closing it would change a number the arm prints.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the decision record entry that fixed Codex's exclusion (Q075).\n2. Read the runner's Codex gate and the `codexHookApproval` verdict mapping.\n3. Read the delivery decision's own documentation of why OpenCode stays unknown.\n4. Read the test that pins OpenCode at unknown.\n5. Read the offer-field accounting that produces `offerUnknown`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. Codex has no rows in the 033 arm because the runner refuses the whole arm, not because its reader failed. When the runtime is codex and `codexHookApproval` reports `unapproved`, the runner writes `{ok:false, code:'codex-hooks-unapproved', measurable:false}` and returns the refused exit before any turn runs, with the repair text \"open /hooks in a Codex session at <dir> and approve each entry\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1473-1488] The operator's answer to Q075 was to leave Codex out of the arm rather than approve it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1486-1499]\n\n2. Approving the Codex hook would not by itself produce a delivery boolean. The reader returns `false` only when the hook is unapproved; otherwise it loads the session and returns `true` when the records or the injected block carry the brief and `unknown` when they do not. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:282-300] So an approved Codex arm whose store does not carry the hook context prints the same `unknown` as OpenCode, and `deliveryUnknown` would not distinguish the two.\n\n3. OpenCode's unknown is a documented design consequence, not an accident: \"OpenCode stays `unknown`, because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\" [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:220-229] That makes a prompt-free receipt necessary but not sufficient: the reader branch must be added too, because the suite currently pins the unknown even for a session whose records do hold the brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:259-265]\n\n4. Devin's and DSH's single unplaceable row each is a run-line format gap, not a runtime behaviour gap. `offerFieldAbsent` is true when the line carries no offer field at all [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1991], and a scored owned row with no offer field is counted into `followedByOffer.unknown` rather than into either side of the offer split [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2375]. The scorer's comment is explicit that such a line was \"written before that field existed\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2363]\n\n5. Ranked by whether closing the gap changes a published number, the reader gaps order as OpenCode, Codex, Devin/DSH. OpenCode carries 80 of 80 run lines at `briefDelivered: unknown` (36 off, 44 on) in its own run log [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/opencode.jsonl] against 0 unknown on claude and pi and 1 on devin and dsh [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt]. Devin and DSH each lose one row to the offer split, which cannot move a rate printed over 28 rows; Codex has 0 rows today, so its fix unlocks a runtime rather than correcting a number. [INFERENCE: from the delivery and offerUnknown counts in summary-arm.json and the per-file unknown tallies above]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating Codex as a sixth measured runtime. No row exists, and the gate that stops it is a runner refusal with an operator repair path, not a scoring gap.\n- Reading the `offerUnknown: 1` on devin and dsh as a lost offer. The field is absent from the line; it is not a recorded non-offer.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching the run logs for opencode rows that carry a delivery answer. All 80 lines read unknown by construction, so no per-row inspection can recover a delivery fact from them.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none. Question (c) named all four cases up front.\n- Contradictory evidence: none, but one asymmetry is worth recording: codex's `false` is a positive answer while opencode's `unknown` is structural, and both are printed under one `deliveryUnknown` field name.\n- Missing dependencies: no Codex session store was read, because no Codex session exists.\n- Partial success: the ranking's first item rests on 80 observed rows; the third rests on a single row per runtime, which is stated as such.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1486-1499`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1465-1499`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:185-229`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:282-303`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1986-1992`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2375`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:232-265`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/opencode.jsonl`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.8\n- Questions addressed: (c)\n- Questions answered: (c)\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading the test beside the reader was decisive. A reader branch alone cannot move OpenCode's number while `command-offer.vitest.ts:259` asserts the unknown for a session that does hold the brief, so the fix has a second file and a second proof that a code-only reading would have missed.\n- What did not work and why: the first attempt to locate the devin and dsh unplaceable rows by scanning every run line for a missing `offeredCommand` returned 51 to 52 lines per runtime, which is the decline and must-not-start population, not the scored set. The scorer's own condition is the only reliable filter, so the finding rests on the accounting rule rather than a row identity.\n- What I would do differently: go to `tallyResult` before scanning logs whenever a count needs attribution. The tally is the definition; the logs only instantiate it.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nQuestion (d): what per-runtime surface decides whether an ask offer is representable. Start from `askedAndWaited` and `ASK_POLICY` in the classifier, then the dsh decline start (`fresh-decline-refusal-02`, `/create:sk-skill` against an offered `/deep:review`) and the devin lost rows that acted with no workflow and no offer.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 2: Every reader gap, ranked by whether a fix would move a published number\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nQuestion (c). Iteration 1 proved that opencode's delivery unknown comes from a missing branch and that the followed rate is a pre-write access test. This iteration enumerates the remaining places where the measuring instrument, not the runtime, sets the limit: codex's exclusion, devin's and dsh's single unplaceable offer row, and opencode's whole arm. Each is then ranked by whether closing it would change a number the arm prints.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the decision record entry that fixed Codex's exclusion (Q075).\\n2. Read the runner's Codex gate and the `codexHookApproval` verdict mapping.\\n3. Read the delivery decision's own documentation of why OpenCode stays unknown.\\n4. Read the test that pins OpenCode at unknown.\\n5. Read the offer-field accounting that produces `offerUnknown`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. Codex has no rows in the 033 arm because the runner refuses the whole arm, not because its reader failed. When the runtime is codex and `codexHookApproval` reports `unapproved`, the runner writes `{ok:false, code:'codex-hooks-unapproved', measurable:false}` and returns the refused exit before any turn runs, with the repair text \\\"open /hooks in a Codex session at <dir> and approve each entry\\\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1473-1488] The operator's answer to Q075 was to leave Codex out of the arm rather than approve it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1486-1499]\\n\\n2. Approving the Codex hook would not by itself produce a delivery boolean. The reader returns `false` only when the hook is unapproved; otherwise it loads the session and returns `true` when the records or the injected block carry the brief and `unknown` when they do not. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:282-300] So an approved Codex arm whose store does not carry the hook context prints the same `unknown` as OpenCode, and `deliveryUnknown` would not distinguish the two.\\n\\n3. OpenCode's unknown is a documented design consequence, not an accident: \\\"OpenCode stays `unknown`, because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\\\" [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:220-229] That makes a prompt-free receipt necessary but not sufficient: the reader branch must be added too, because the suite currently pins the unknown even for a session whose records do hold the brief. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:259-265]\\n\\n4. Devin's and DSH's single unplaceable row each is a run-line format gap, not a runtime behaviour gap. `offerFieldAbsent` is true when the line carries no offer field at all [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1991], and a scored owned row with no offer field is counted into `followedByOffer.unknown` rather than into either side of the offer split [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2375]. The scorer's comment is explicit that such a line was \\\"written before that field existed\\\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2363]\\n\\n5. Ranked by whether closing the gap changes a published number, the reader gaps order as OpenCode, Codex, Devin/DSH. OpenCode carries 80 of 80 run lines at `briefDelivered: unknown` (36 off, 44 on) in its own run log [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/opencode.jsonl] against 0 unknown on claude and pi and 1 on devin and dsh [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt]. Devin and DSH each lose one row to the offer split, which cannot move a rate printed over 28 rows; Codex has 0 rows today, so its fix unlocks a runtime rather than correcting a number. [INFERENCE: from the delivery and offerUnknown counts in summary-arm.json and the per-file unknown tallies above]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating Codex as a sixth measured runtime. No row exists, and the gate that stops it is a runner refusal with an operator repair path, not a scoring gap.\\n- Reading the `offerUnknown: 1` on devin and dsh as a lost offer. The field is absent from the line; it is not a recorded non-offer.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching the run logs for opencode rows that carry a delivery answer. All 80 lines read unknown by construction, so no per-row inspection can recover a delivery fact from them.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: none. Question (c) named all four cases up front.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none, but one asymmetry is worth recording: codex's `false` is a positive answer while opencode's `unknown` is structural, and both are printed under one `deliveryUnknown` field name.\\n- Missing dependencies: no Codex session store was read, because no Codex session exists.\\n- Partial success: the ranking's first item rests on 80 observed rows; the third rests on a single row per runtime, which is stated as such.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1486-1499`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1465-1499`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:185-229`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:282-303`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1986-1992`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2375`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:232-265`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/opencode.jsonl`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.8\\n- Questions addressed: (c)\\n- Questions answered: (c)\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: reading the test beside the reader was decisive. A reader branch alone cannot move OpenCode's number while `command-offer.vitest.ts:259` asserts the unknown for a session that does hold the brief, so the fix has a second file and a second proof that a code-only reading would have missed.\\n- What did not work and why: the first attempt to locate the devin and dsh unplaceable rows by scanning every run line for a missing `offeredCommand` returned 51 to 52 lines per runtime, which is the decline and must-not-start population, not the scored set. The scorer's own condition is the only reliable filter, so the finding rests on the accounting rule rather than a row identity.\\n- What I would do differently: go to `tallyResult` before scanning logs whenever a count needs attribution. The tally is the definition; the logs only instantiate it.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nQuestion (d): what per-runtime surface decides whether an ask offer is representable. Start from `askedAndWaited` and `ASK_POLICY` in the classifier, then the dsh decline start (`fresh-decline-refusal-02`, `/create:sk-skill` against an offered `/deep:review`) and the devin lost rows that acted with no workflow and no offer.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801703318,"end":1794801720176}}}}
