napproved and otherwise unknown unless the session records or injected block carry the brief, so an approved Codex arm can print the same unknown as OpenCode.\", sources: [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:282-300\"] },\n  { id: \"f-iter002-003\", label: \"OpenCode unknown is documented as design: the plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy, and the suite pins unknown even for a session whose records hold the brief at command-offer.vitest.ts:259-265, so a receipt alone would not move the number.\", sources: [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:220-229\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts:259-265\"] },\n  { id: \"f-iter002-004\", label: \"The devin and dsh single offerUnknown row is a run-line format gap: offerFieldAbsent is true when the line carries no offer field and a scored owned row is then counted apart rather than as a non-offer.\", sources: [\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1991\", \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2361-2375\"] },\n  { id: \"f-iter002-005\", label: \"Reader gaps rank OpenCode then Codex then Devin/DSH by published-number impact: OpenCode carries 80 of 80 lines unknown, Devin and DSH lose one row each which cannot move a rate over 28, and Codex has 0 rows so its fix unlocks a runtime rather than correcting a number.\", sources: [\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/runs/opencode.jsonl\", \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt\"] }\n];\nconst lines = [JSON.stringify(record)];\nfor (const f of findings) lines.push(JSON.stringify({ type: \"finding\", id: f.id, label: f.label, iteration: 2, sources: f.sources }));\nfs.writeFileSync(dir + \"/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\", lines.join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\");\nconst tmp = fs.mkdtempSync(require(\"os\").tmpdir() + \"/dr5-i2-\");\nfs.writeFileSync(tmp + \"/event.json\", JSON.stringify(record));\nprocess.stdout.write(tmp + \"/event.json\\n\");\n' \"$LINEAGE\""},"output":"/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/dr5-i2-w6DRdL/event.json\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/dr5-i2-w6DRdL/event.json\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && LINEAGE=\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5\\\" && node -e '\\nconst fs = require(\\\"fs\\\");\\nconst dir = process.argv[1];\\nconst sid = \\\"fanout-cross-cli-5-1794801313778-3ys69o\\\";\\nconst qc = \\\"(c) Which runtimes still have a reader or attribution gap the arm cannot see — codex unmeasured under Q075, devin and dsh one unknown row each, opencode all unknown — and what file line proves each gap?\\\";\\nconst record = {\\n  type: \\\"iteration\\\", iteration: 2, runId: sid, sessionId: sid, lineageId: sid,\\n  mode: \\\"research\\\", target_agent: \\\"deep-research\\\", agent_definition_loaded: true,\\n  resolved_route: \\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\n  run: 2, status: \\\"complete\\\",\\n  focus: \\\"Every reader gap, ranked by whether a fix would move a published number\\\",\\n  findingsCount: 5, newInfoRatio: 0.8,\\n  noveltyJustification: \\\"4 of 5 findings are new file-line proofs (the Codex refusal gate, the approved-Codex unknown, the pinned OpenCode test, the offer-field accounting); the ranking restates counts already seen.\\\",\\n  k