{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794801978236,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"id":"prt_1e288cb7c001ALBWYCy9kv6RrP","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e2889ab9001w0l9w05QD0NQXx","type":"step-start","snapshot":"37f90633c6013e0d75d917f9af3bc83b98afc2b4"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794801996321,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e288d9b6002JpUrc5X4Yr5AKy","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e2889ab9001w0l9w05QD0NQXx","type":"tool","id":"call_68d4c0f44f6049179a4da770","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: What a \"start\" is on each runtime, and why the two start functions disagree\n\n## Focus\n\nThe rank from iteration 4 rests on rows and files. Before synthesizing, the arm's other headline number needs the same treatment the followed rate got: the start rate. This iteration asked what evidence makes a run count as started, whether every runtime can produce that evidence, and whether the two functions that judge a start agree with each other.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `startState`, the function behind the printed start rate.\n2. Read `startedCommand`, the function behind the decline and skill-only start counts.\n3. Read the comment that defines Claude's host-expansion start shape.\n4. Traced both values to the fields the summary prints.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. A start row counts as started without any write. `startState` sets `started` from a document read, a model-reported `COMMAND:` start line, or a host expansion, and never consults a write boundary. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493] The start rate therefore answers \"did the run open the command's document or say it started\", not \"did it do the work\".\n\n2. The two start functions disagree about a bare document read. For a decline or skill-only row, `startedCommand` accepts a document read only when a write boundary exists; the same read with no write is not a start there. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1424-1441] So one transcript can be a start under the start rate and not a start under the decline count, and both numbers appear in the same runtime block.\n\n3. The start vocabulary is runtime-asymmetric. `hostExpanded` recognises Claude Code's expansion tag, which exists because Claude expands a typed command before the model sees it and keeps only that tag in the stored user turn; the comment records the consequence that it \"is not a spoken command: the model never chose it\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1395-1402] Claude is the only one of the six runtimes that can produce this event, so its start count can include a start the model did not choose while the other five cannot.\n\n4. Nothing in the summary prints which shape produced a start, so the mix cannot be recovered after the fact. `byPolicy` carries counts only [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2399-2403], and `commandStartRuns` lists the row, the run and the command but not the shape [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2300-2304]. With 15 judged start rows per runtime per arm, a two-row difference between claude's 2 and 3 could be one read and one expansion in either order.\n\n5. The fix is a measurement field, not a product change: record the shape (read, reported, expanded, skill) on each scored row and print its distribution per runtime. That would make claude's 2 of 15 and 3 of 15, opencode's 1 of 7 and 3 of 10, pi's 3 of 14 and 6 of 15, devin's 2 of 11 and 6 of 12 and dsh's 6 of 15 and 10 of 15 comparable quantities rather than five differently-earned numerators. No command, vector, brief byte or floor input changes. [INFERENCE: from findings 1 to 4 and the start counts in summary-arm.json]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating the printed start rate as \"the model took the workflow\". A document read alone earns it, and on Claude an expansion the model never chose also earns it.\n- Comparing runtimes on start rate without naming the shape mix, while the shape vocabulary differs by runtime.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Searching the run logs for a start-shape field. No such field exists in the line schema; only `changedPaths`, `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `briefDelivered`, `restored` and `exit` are written.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none.\n- Contradictory evidence: the two start functions are not contradictory, but they are inconsistent measures of the same word; both are recorded here and the inconsistency is named rather than resolved.\n- Missing dependencies: no transcript-level shape census was run, because that would require re-reading 400 session files for a number the summary cannot print anyway.\n- Partial success: the shape fix is proposed without a measurement of how much of each runtime's start count is a read. That is stated as the confirming step rather than assumed.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1424-1441`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1395-1402`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2300-2304`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2399-2403`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.7\n- Questions addressed: (e) follow-on, start-credit attribution\n- Questions answered: none as tracked; this closes a gap the rank opened\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading the second start function paid off. The discrepancy between `startState` and `startedCommand` over a bare read is invisible in any printed table and changes what both numbers mean, so one function would have looked consistent while two disagreed.\n- What did not work and why: the first attempt to identify the start rows by row id found none, because the rows are keyed by policy rather than by a `fresh-start-*` name. The policy key is the right handle and it is what `isStartRow` uses.\n- What I would do differently: read `startState` and `startedCommand` in the same pass from the beginning. Any two functions that print a field called \"started\" in one block should be read together.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAudit the six inherited `limit:` lines in `arm-evidence.txt` against the 033 counts. They came from phase 026 and one of them (\"devin on-arm lost rows acted with no workflow and no offer\") does not obviously match 033's devin block, where `improvised` is 0 in both arms. A stale limit line is a reading hazard for every downstream synthesis.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Iteration 5: What a \\\"start\\\" is on each runtime, and why the two start functions disagree\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nThe rank from iteration 4 rests on rows and files. Before synthesizing, the arm's other headline number needs the same treatment the followed rate got: the start rate. This iteration asked what evidence makes a run count as started, whether every runtime can produce that evidence, and whether the two functions that judge a start agree with each other.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `startState`, the function behind the printed start rate.\\n2. Read `startedCommand`, the function behind the decline and skill-only start counts.\\n3. Read the comment that defines Claude's host-expansion start shape.\\n4. Traced both values to the fields the summary prints.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. A start row counts as started without any write. `startState` sets `started` from a document read, a model-reported `COMMAND:` start line, or a host expansion, and never consults a write boundary. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493] The start rate therefore answers \\\"did the run open the command's document or say it started\\\", not \\\"did it do the work\\\".\\n\\n2. The two start functions disagree about a bare document read. For a decline or skill-only row, `startedCommand` accepts a document read only when a write boundary exists; the same read with no write is not a start there. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1424-1441] So one transcript can be a start under the start rate and not a start under the decline count, and both numbers appear in the same runtime block.\\n\\n3. The start vocabulary is runtime-asymmetric. `hostExpanded` recognises Claude Code's expansion tag, which exists because Claude expands a typed command before the model sees it and keeps only that tag in the stored user turn; the comment records the consequence that it \\\"is not a spoken command: the model never chose it\\\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1395-1402] Claude is the only one of the six runtimes that can produce this event, so its start count can include a start the model did not choose while the other five cannot.\\n\\n4. Nothing in the summary prints which shape produced a start, so the mix cannot be recovered after the fact. `byPolicy` carries counts only [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2399-2403], and `commandStartRuns` lists the row, the run and the command but not the shape [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2300-2304]. With 15 judged start rows per runtime per arm, a two-row difference between claude's 2 and 3 could be one read and one expansion in either order.\\n\\n5. The fix is a measurement field, not a product change: record the shape (read, reported, expanded, skill) on each scored row and print its distribution per runtime. That would make claude's 2 of 15 and 3 of 15, opencode's 1 of 7 and 3 of 10, pi's 3 of 14 and 6 of 15, devin's 2 of 11 and 6 of 12 and dsh's 6 of 15 and 10 of 15 comparable quantities rather than five differently-earned numerators. No command, vector, brief byte or floor input changes. [INFERENCE: from findings 1 to 4 and the start counts in summary-arm.json]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating the printed start rate as \\\"the model took the workflow\\\". A document read alone earns it, and on Claude an expansion the model never chose also earns it.\\n- Comparing runtimes on start rate without naming the shape mix, while the shape vocabulary differs by runtime.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Searching the run logs for a start-shape field. No such field exists in the line schema; only `changedPaths`, `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy`, `offeredAs`, `briefDelivered`, `restored` and `exit` are written.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: none.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the two start functions are not contradictory, but they are inconsistent measures of the same word; both are recorded here and the inconsistency is named rather than resolved.\\n- Missing dependencies: no transcript-level shape census was run, because that would require re-reading 400 session files for a number the summary cannot print anyway.\\n- Partial success: the shape fix is proposed without a measurement of how much of each runtime's start count is a read. That is stated as the confirming step rather than assumed.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1424-1441`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1395-1402`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2300-2304`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:2399-2403`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.7\\n- Questions addressed: (e) follow-on, start-credit attribution\\n- Questions answered: none as tracked; this closes a gap the rank opened\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: reading the second start function paid off. The discrepancy between `startState` and `startedCommand` over a bare read is invisible in any printed table and changes what both numbers mean, so one function would have looked consistent while two disagreed.\\n- What did not work and why: the first attempt to identify the start rows by row id found none, because the rows are keyed by policy rather than by a `fresh-start-*` name. The policy key is the right handle and it is what `isStartRow` uses.\\n- What I would do differently: read `startState` and `startedCommand` in the same pass from the beginning. Any two functions that print a field called \\\"started\\\" in one block should be read together.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAudit the six inherited `limit:` lines in `arm-evidence.txt` against the 033 counts. They came from phase 026 and one of them (\\\"devin on-arm lost rows acted with no workflow and no offer\\\") does not obviously match 033's devin block, where `improvised` is 0 in both arms. A stale limit line is a reading hazard for every downstream synthesis.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794801981878,"end":1794801996321}}}}
