{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794802346345,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"partID":"prt_1e28e6267002vEZhxhu1xkxy7j","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e28e54ab001j0HLUsS4uVsWAQ","type":"tool","id":"call_eeb26d56856148d588697ef5","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md","oldString":"8. What remains unmeasured in this lane: whether a longer OpenCode cap would raise its judgeable rows (the `performance-5` lane owns the cap itself); whether Claude's home rules file moves any row (item 5 is the test, not yet run); and which shape produced each existing start count (item 2 is the test). No claim in this lane rests on those three, and each is stated as a proposed measurement rather than a result.","newString":"8. What remains unmeasured in this lane: whether a longer OpenCode cap would raise its judgeable rows (the `performance-5` lane owns the cap itself); whether Claude's home rules file moves any row (item 5 is the test, not yet run); and which shape produced each existing start count (item 2 is the test). No claim in this lane rests on those three, and each is stated as a proposed measurement rather than a result. [INFERENCE: from the capped and start counts in summary-arm.json and the files named in items 2 and 5]"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md\n@@ -26,9 +26,9 @@\n 6. The lane's final order, each with file and check. (1) The OpenCode receipt plus reader branch: `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` after the emitted-block observer, an `opencode` branch in `command-offer.mjs` `briefDelivered`, and the test at `command-offer.vitest.ts:259-265`; confirmed when the next arm's OpenCode off rows read `briefDelivered: false` and its `offerReached` reads 0 of 5 against 5 of 5 on, where today both read 5 of 5. (2) The start-shape field and its per-runtime distribution in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`; confirmed by a printed shape count per runtime. (3) The `capped` split into exit 143 and exit null; confirmed by devin's start rate printing over 15 rows instead of 11 and 12, and by a `capped` line that names its cause. (4) `restored: false` scored as unscored with a reason; confirmed by dsh's `unscored` rising from 0 to 1 and devin's by 2. (5) One Claude arm with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` on an empty directory; confirmed by a same-rows followed comparison against 6 of 28. (6) The Codex arm unlock, blocked on the operator's `/hooks` approval rather than on code. (7) The ask-representation widening, which touches 1 of 280 runs and rewrites prior arms' numbers. [INFERENCE: assembled from iterations 2 to 7]\n \n 7. Floor risk is none for items 1 to 5 and 7's product side, because none of them changes a command, a vector, a brief byte or a scoring input: items 1 to 4 are readers and counters, 5 is a run setting, and 6 is an operator action. Item 7 changes a measure, which is why it is last, and it would alter previously published arm numbers if adopted retroactively. [INFERENCE: from the file list and the recorded floors of 24 of 44 typed and 0 of 35 false offers]\n \n-8. What remains unmeasured in this lane: whether a longer OpenCode cap would raise its judgeable rows (the `performance-5` lane owns the cap itself); whether Claude's home rules file moves any row (item 5 is the test, not yet run); and which shape produced each existing start count (item 2 is the test). No claim in this lane rests on those three, and each is stated as a proposed measurement rather than a result.\n+8. What remains unmeasured in this lane: whether a longer OpenCode cap would raise its judgeable rows (the `performance-5` lane owns the cap itself); whether Claude's home rules file moves any row (item 5 is the test, not yet run); and which shape produced each existing start count (item 2 is the test). No claim in this lane rests on those three, and each is stated as a proposed measurement rather than a result. [INFERENCE: from the capped and start counts in summary-arm.json and the files named in items 2 and 5]\n \n ## Ruled Out\n \n - A sixth answer question. The lane's five questions are answered; the four extra findings are measurement facts about the instrument, and folding them into a new question would hide that they were found while testing the answers.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5/iterations/iteration-008.md\",\"oldString\":\"8. What remains unmeasured in this lane: whether a longer OpenCode cap would raise its judgeable rows (the `performance-5` lane owns the cap itself); whether Claude's home rules file moves any row (item 5 is the test, not yet run); and which shape produced each existing start count (item 2 is the test). No claim in this lane rests on those three, and each is stated as a proposed measurement rather than a result.\",\"newString\":\"8. What remains unmeasured in this lane: whether a longer OpenCode cap would raise its judgeable rows (the `performance-5` lane owns the cap itself); whether Claude's home rules file moves any row (item 5 is the test, not yet run); and which shape produced each existing start count (item 2 is the test). No claim in this lane rests on those three, and each is stated as a proposed measurement rather than a result. [INFERENCE: from the capped and start counts in summary-arm.json and the files named in items 2 and 5]\"}"},"time":{"start":1794802344551,"end":1794802346345}}}}
