{"type":"text","timestamp":1794802388355,"sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","part":{"id":"prt_1e28efd4c0020eMEgjwBxWorSX","sessionID":"ses_e1d81443fffeGbe5CDTKaTeXws","messageID":"msg_1e28ef245001zLzxD8xV5d83Cn","type":"text","text":"Lane complete. Summary of what stands on disk in `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-5`:\n\n**Run**: 8 iterations, ratio trend 0.75 → 0.35, stopped at `maxIterationsReached` with 5 of 5 key questions answered. Ledger holds 10 receipts (run-open, 8 iterations, synthesis-complete); config status `complete`; reducer reports 8 iterations, 0 corruption, 45 key findings.\n\n**What the arm can actually say per runtime** — the lane's core result:\n- `followed` and `started` are both pre-write document-access tests (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:1182-1212`, `:1477-1493`), so the 4-of-28 to 24-of-28 spread is access, not execution. Phase 033's step reader gives the execution counterpart: setup 15/20, folder 12/20, output **4/20**, and its runtime order inverts the arm's.\n- OpenCode's 80 delivery-unknown rows are a missing reader, not a delivery failure (`command-offer.mjs:239-303`), and because `unknown` counts as offer-reached (`:2351-2353`) its off-arm counterfactual is erased — the four reader runtimes read `offerReached` 0 of 5 → 5 of 5, OpenCode 5 of 5 → 5 of 5.\n- `capped` means exit 143 on OpenCode (26 rows) and exit `null` on Devin (19 rows), and `restored`/`headMoved` are never read, so a head-moving row the runner calls unmeasurable is scored (`:1998-1999`, `:2035-2038`).\n- The offer field is a replay in both arms; Claude additionally carries a 27,730-byte home rules file the harness never isolates.\n- The dsh decline-row start is a policy outcome, not a representation loss: the offer arrived, was declined twelve times, and a different command started anyway.\n\n**Ranked**: OpenCode receipt + reader branch → start-shape field → `capped` split → restore-failure scoring → Claude isolation arm → Codex unlock → ask-representation widening. None of the first five touches a command, vector, brief byte or scoring input.\n\n**Operator note**: nothing here needs your action; item 6 (Codex) stays waiting on the `/hooks` approval already recorded under Q075.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:cross-cli-5","time":{"start":1794802384204,"end":1794802388355}}}
